{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01RPwYcXNNmywUkrQuX3vdRA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/04-007-scalable-efficient-llm-training-system-compute-and-data-cons.md`** — here's what it covers:\n\n**Q7: Scalable efficient LLM training system — compute and data constraints** (Senior-level design question)\n\n**Three co-designed subsystems:**\n1. **Parallelism strategy** — DDP + ZeRO Stage 2 (DeepSpeed/FSDP) as the production default for 7B–70B fine-tuning; 3D parallelism (Tensor + Pipeline + Data) for 100B+ pre-training à la Megatron-LM. Includes a decision table comparing DDP / TP / PP / ZeRO with overhead tradeoffs.\n2. **Memory optimization stack** — BF16 mixed precision, gradient checkpointing (~33% compute overhead → 60–70% activation memory savings → 2× batch size), FlashAttention 2 for long-context (O(n²)→O(n)), ZeRO-Offload for 30B+ on a single node.\n3. **Data pipeline** — pre-tokenize offline into Arrow/WebDataset shards, stream from S3/GCS, 16 DataLoader workers per node, MinHash LSH dedup, quality classifiers, Chinchilla's 20 tokens/param budget rule (7B → 140B tokens).\n\n**Key pitfalls covered:** Not naming a parallelism strategy; ignoring the data pipeline; treating gradient checkpointing as \"free.\"\n\n6 items remain in the Next queue (Q8–Q12 + validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":68818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":293,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"445369af-b17f-4bbf-8a85-c47108b35571","uuid":"0a96e982-3576-4848-ac69-1bb3a10ffa73"}
